== C. tetrahedral duality ==
PASS C1 all 64: c3(T) = #sources+#sinks of T*
PASS C2 all 64: #sources+#sinks of T = c3(T*)
PASS C3 all 64: H(T*) = 6 - H(T)
PASS C4 T** is always the same one of {T, T^op}  [{'T'}]
PASS C5 duality on types: TT4 <-> strong, and the two C3 types stay inside the C3 class  [{'TT4': {'strong'}, 'C3+sink': {'C3+sink', 'C3+source'}, 'strong': {'TT4'}, 'C3+source': {'C3+sink', 'C3+source'}}]
PASS C6 converse on types: C3+source <-> C3+sink, TT4 and strong fixed  [{'TT4': {'TT4'}, 'C3+sink': {'C3+source'}, 'strong': {'strong'}, 'C3+source': {'C3+sink'}}]
PASS C7 (T^op)* = (T*)^op on all 64 (converse and duality commute)
PASS C8 the dual arc of u->v lies on the opposite edge of the tetrahedron

